# Context fidelity

Before writing, read `skills/maintain-context/SKILL.md` and only the reference for this situation.

A fact that is `accepted` cites a source that was read: a path, a manifest, a script, or the output of a command, and when it was read. With no source, the statement is a hypothesis and stays `proposed`. What was not read is the words "not observed". Do not invent a purpose, a layer, a stack, a container, or an Evans relation.

The index is short. A later task opens the accepted index and the one slice it needs. `/context-start` writes one pointer sentence into `AGENTS.md` so that task can find the index. It does not write a rule file.

Several projects stay separate. The map records a relation only when a source shows it.

A change is the next `<NNN>`. The previous row becomes `superseded`. Do not rewrite an `accepted` file unless the person asks to amend that same file.

A recommendation starts `proposed`. Name the plugin and the signal. Do not install it and do not copy its skill.

A folder is suite output only when its `ORIGIN.json` was read and `suite` is `ADRenaline-Suite`. Read that file in each direct child of the project root, in each direct child of `adrenaline/`, and in each `outputDirs` path. A path found twice is one row. Do not walk any other directory. Record the folder, the plugin, and that file on the index. Do not infer it from the folder name. Do not copy those artifacts into the index. Do not install the plugin because the folder exists.

The architecture description and the ADR belong to `plugin-software-architect`. The drawing belongs to `plugin-uml-diagrams`. The domain model belongs to `plugin-backend`. The reader-facing document belongs to `plugin-documentation`. Retrieval for a model belongs to `plugin-genai`. The use case belongs to `plugin-project-manager`.

The session hook may add `drift:` in `notas`. It does not write a snapshot and it does not change `estado`.
